  "body": "Found by the review of PR #1099 (#1071), comment on head 434a464a (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/1099). It is pre-existing on main and not on that PR's path. Filed by an agent for a contributor, who can't set labels. Suggested labels: `bug`, `P1` (a gouge that passes), `effort:high` (gouge law, safety floor), `area:verify`, `source:agent`.\n\n**What happens.** The containment kinds' solid law excuses a hole-wall facet hit by its chord dip (`crates/sim/src/verify/swept.rs`, `chord_dip`, used from `solid_index.rs` when `hole_walls` is set):\n- a facet whose three vertices all stand outside the atom's widest reach along the move is credited `rho - sqrt(rho^2 - half^2)` for each edge shorter than the atom's diameter;\n- that reads every such facet as the inscribed tessellation of a round wall that the region's exact rim already judged.\n\nA hole that really is a coarse polygon has flats that dip well inside the circle through its corners, and they get the same credit. Those flats are real material, not tessellation.\n\n**Reproduction (from the review):**\n- The fixture: #1071's `thread_mill_rim` block with an octagonal blind hole, vertices on r 5, so the flats stand at r 4.62.\n- A model-sourced Thread op declared at r 4.4, with a 6 mm Tap-form thread mill at pitch 1.\n- Its major circle is 4.94, off #1099's thread-wall band, so #1099's grant does not apply.\n- Result: the verify gives no blocking warning, and the helix cuts about 0.32 mm into each flat. The chord dip for a 3 mm atom on the flats' 3.83 mm chords is about 0.69 mm.\n\nThe review expects a Bore on a coarse polygon hole to behave the same way. That has not been reproduced yet.\n\n**What should happen.** The excuse should credit only tessellation of a round wall: a dip bounded by a stated mesh tolerance, as #1099 does for the thread grant (`CHORD_CREDIT` = `DEV_TOL`, 0.01 mm; the STEP importer meshes at half of it). It should not credit any chord shorter than the cutter.\n\n**Done means:**\n- an octagon (and a 16-gon) hole cut past its flats by a containment kind (Bore, and Thread off the band) convicts;\n- a full-fidelity round hole (a fine 96-gon) still verifies clean for every containment kind;\n- both are pinned by tests;\n- `solid_law`, `solid_law_goldens`, `bore_facet_sagitta` and `golden_cl` stay green.\n",
